CHAPTER 2: PROJECT MODULE DESCRIPTION
3.1 INTRODUCTION
The Ai Mock Interviewer system is designed with a modular architecture that divides the overall functionality into well-defined, independent, and interrelated modules. Each module is responsible for a specific aspect of the system, ensuring clarity in design, ease of development, and maintainability. The modular approach also facilitates testing and debugging, as each component can be verified independently before integration.
This chapter provides a comprehensive description of all the project modules, their individual responsibilities, inter-module dependencies, and how they collectively contribute to the functioning of the complete system.
3.2 MODULE OVERVIEW
The system comprises the following core modules:
•	User Authentication Module
•	Interview Management Module
•	AI Question Generation Module
•	Answer Evaluation Module
•	Analytics and Performance Tracking Module
•	Frontend User Interface Module
•	Database Management Module
Each module operates as a self-contained unit with well-defined inputs, outputs, and interfaces.
3.3 USER AUTHENTICATION MODULE
Purpose:
The User Authentication Module handles user registration, login, and secure session management. It ensures that only authorized users can access the system and its features.
Key Functions:
•	User registration with input validation (name, email, password).
•	Secure login with credential verification.
•	Password hashing using bcrypt for safe storage.
•	JWT (JSON Web Token) generation for stateless session management.
•	Profile retrieval for authenticated users.
•	Middleware-based route protection for secured endpoints.
Module Dependencies:
•	Database Management Module (for storing and retrieving user data).
•	Frontend UI Module (for login/signup forms).
3.4 INTERVIEW MANAGEMENT MODULE
Purpose:
The Interview Management Module is responsible for creating, managing, and organizing interview sessions. It acts as the central coordinator between user preferences and AI-driven functionalities.
Key Functions:
•	Creating new interview sessions based on user-selected parameters (job role, domain, difficulty level).
•	Storing interview session details in the database.
•	Managing the lifecycle of an interview from creation to completion.
•	Retrieving interview history for user review.
•	Coordinating with the AI Question Generation Module and Answer Evaluation Module.
Module Dependencies:
•	AI Question Generation Module (for generating questions).
•	Answer Evaluation Module (for evaluating responses).
•	Database Management Module (for persisting interview data).
3.5 AI QUESTION GENERATION MODULE
Purpose:
The AI Question Generation Module leverages the Groq API and Large Language Models (LLaMA, Mixtral) to dynamically generate customized interview questions based on user inputs.
Key Functions:
•	Accepting user-defined parameters such as job title, domain, experience level, and difficulty.
•	Constructing structured prompts for the AI model.
•	Sending API requests to the Groq API for question generation.
•	Receiving and parsing AI-generated questions.
•	Supporting multiple question types: Technical, Behavioral, and Scenario-based.
•	Implementing fallback mechanisms in case of API failure.
Module Dependencies:
•	Groq API (external AI service).
•	Interview Management Module (for providing user preferences).
3.6 ANSWER EVALUATION MODULE
Purpose:
The Answer Evaluation Module processes user responses and provides intelligent, AI-driven feedback. It uses semantic analysis to evaluate answers beyond simple keyword matching.
Key Functions:
•	Receiving user answers from the frontend.
•	Constructing evaluation prompts incorporating the question, user response, and job context.
•	Sending evaluation requests to the Groq API.
•	Parsing AI-generated evaluation results including scores, feedback, and improvement suggestions.
•	Storing evaluation results in the database.
Module Dependencies:
•	Groq API (for AI-based evaluation).
•	Interview Management Module (for question and interview context).
•	Database Management Module (for storing evaluation results).
3.7 ANALYTICS AND PERFORMANCE TRACKING MODULE
Purpose:
The Analytics Module tracks user performance across multiple interview sessions and provides data-driven insights for continuous improvement.
Key Functions:
•	Recording scores and feedback from each interview session.
•	Calculating performance metrics and trends over time.
•	Generating user-specific analytics reports.
•	Providing overall performance summaries.
•	Identifying strengths and areas for improvement.
Module Dependencies:
•	Database Management Module (for retrieving historical performance data).
•	Answer Evaluation Module (for feeding evaluation results).
3.8 FRONTEND USER INTERFACE MODULE
Purpose:
The Frontend UI Module provides the presentation layer of the system, offering an interactive and user-friendly interface for all system functionalities.
Key Functions:
•	Rendering login/signup forms for user authentication.
•	Displaying the dashboard for initiating interviews.
•	Presenting AI-generated interview questions.
•	Accepting and submitting user responses.
•	Displaying evaluation results, scores, and feedback.
•	Showing performance analytics and progress charts.
•	Handling client-side input validation.
Module Dependencies:
•	All backend modules (via RESTful API communication).
3.9 DATABASE MANAGEMENT MODULE
Purpose:
The Database Management Module handles all data storage, retrieval, and management operations using MySQL as the relational database management system.
Key Functions:
•	Managing user data (registration, credentials, profiles).
•	Storing interview sessions with associated parameters.
•	Persisting AI-generated questions and user answers.
•	Recording evaluation scores and feedback.
•	Supporting efficient querying for analytics and reporting.
•	Ensuring data integrity through foreign key constraints and validation.
Module Dependencies:
•	Backend server (Node.js/Express.js for database connectivity).
3.10 MODULE INTERACTION DIAGRAM
The modules interact with each other in a well-defined sequence to deliver the complete interview experience:
1.	The User Authentication Module verifies the user identity and grants access.
2.	The Interview Management Module receives user preferences and initiates the session.
3.	The AI Question Generation Module produces relevant interview questions.
4.	The Frontend UI Module displays questions and accepts user answers.
5.	The Answer Evaluation Module processes responses and generates feedback.
6.	The Analytics Module records performance data for tracking.
7.	The Database Management Module supports all modules with persistent data storage.
This interconnected design ensures a seamless, end-to-end user experience.
3.11 SUMMARY
This chapter provided a detailed description of all the project modules in the Ai Mock Interviewer system. Each module was described with its purpose, key functions, and dependencies. The modular architecture ensures that the system is maintainable, scalable, and efficient. The clear separation of concerns allows independent development, testing, and enhancement of each module, contributing to the overall robustness and reliability of the system.


CHAPTER 3: DEPLOYMENT ENVIRONMENT
4.1 INTRODUCTION
The deployment environment defines the infrastructure, tools, platforms, and configurations required to host and run the Ai Mock Interviewer system in a production setting. A well-planned deployment environment is essential to ensure that the application is accessible, reliable, secure, and scalable for end users. This chapter describes the hardware and software requirements, hosting platforms, deployment architecture, and configuration strategies employed for deploying the system.
4.2 DEPLOYMENT ARCHITECTURE
The Ai Mock Interviewer system follows a distributed deployment architecture where different components of the application are hosted independently to ensure modularity and scalability.
The deployment architecture consists of:
•	Frontend Deployment: The client-side application (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) is deployed as a static website on a hosting platform.
•	Backend Deployment: The server-side application (Node.js, Express.js) is deployed on a cloud-based or dedicated server.
•	Database Deployment: The MySQL database is hosted either locally or on a cloud-based database service.
•	AI API Service: The Groq API is accessed as an external cloud-based service for AI-driven functionalities.
This separation ensures that each component can be independently scaled, updated, and maintained without affecting the other components.
4.3 HARDWARE REQUIREMENTS FOR DEPLOYMENT
The system does not require specialized hardware and can be deployed on standard computing infrastructure.
Server Requirements:
•	CPU: Dual-core processor or higher.
•	RAM: Minimum 4 GB (8 GB recommended for production).
•	Storage: Minimum 10 GB of available disk space.
•	Network: Stable internet connection with adequate bandwidth for API communication.
Client Requirements:
•	Any modern computing device (desktop, laptop, tablet, or smartphone).
•	A compatible web browser (Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Microsoft Edge, Safari).
•	Active internet connection.
